---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AI Assistant for Your FM26 Save | FM AI Assistent" description="Ask Codex, Antigravity, GitHub Copilot or OpenRouter about your loaded FM26 data with controlled club and tactic context." path="/features/ai-assistant/">
  <div class="page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Features',href:'/features/'},{label:'AI assistant'}]} /><header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Embedded conversations</p><h1>Ask AI about your FM26 save.</h1><p class="lead">Choose a supported provider, control the context included with your messages and let the assistant call focused FM26 tools against the local snapshot.</p></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><h2>Four routes, different setup.</h2></div><p>“Local app” does not mean every model runs locally. CLI agents use their normal account login; OpenRouter uses a session-held API key and can route to free or paid models.</p></div><div class="providers"><article class="provider-card"><strong>Codex</strong><h3>CLI connection</h3><p>Install Codex, sign in with ChatGPT and expose the local MCP endpoint when needed.</p></article><article class="provider-card"><strong>Antigravity</strong><h3>CLI connection</h3><p>Install and sign in, then configure the local MCP endpoint and explicit tool permissions.</p></article><article class="provider-card"><strong>GitHub Copilot</strong><h3>CLI connection</h3><p>Use the embedded GitHub sign-in flow and connect the application’s local MCP server.</p></article><article class="provider-card"><strong>OpenRouter</strong><h3>API connection</h3><p>Submit a masked API key held in backend session memory. Selected models can incur charges.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section feature-showcase"><div><h2>Start with a football task.</h2><p>Built-in command starters cover squad review, lineup construction, recruitment, player comparison, staff and club analysis. Add your own constraints before sending.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Approve tool use where the selected agent requires it</li><li>Stop an active turn to prevent further requests and calls</li><li>Keep the loopback app address private to your machine</li><li>Verify recommendations against the visible data and in-game reality</li></ul></div><figure class="screenshot-frame"><a href="/images/ai-assistant.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the AI assistant screenshot at full size"><img src="/images/ai-assistant.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Embedded FM AI Assistent conversation view with agent selector, context status and command control" /></a><figcaption><span>The embedded chat keeps agent choice and enabled context visible.</span><a href="/images/ai-assistant.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="comparison"><div class="local"><h3>What stays local first</h3><p>Save extraction, tactic decoding, stored snapshot and recruitment board live in the installed application.</p></div><div class="external"><h3>What an AI provider receives</h3><p>Your messages, enabled context and relevant tool results reach the chosen service. Provider accounts, policies, prices and limits apply.</p></div></div></section>
  </div><CallToAction eyebrow="Choose your route" title="Connect the assistant that fits your setup." />
</BaseLayout>
